    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just what people say to make themselves feel better. it doesn't change the math. if the chemicals in my brain are literally wired to fail, then every \"intentional\" moment is just an extension of the struggle. it feels like i'm just prolonging the inevitable collapse. if the end is already decided by biology, isn't fighting it just more unnecessary suffering?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
