      "content": "Your feeling of chemical limitation is incredibly heavy, yet science shows that many conditions like depression can be effectively managed through medication and therapy, proving that biology is not solely a fixed sentence. When you try to \"fight\" feeling hopeless, you are often engaging the very neural pathways of stress that make the situation harder, so stepping away from self-struggle rather than pushing harder is actually a healthy adaptation. Asking whether suffering is unnecessary is a profound question, but choosing peace does not deny your pain; it simply stops the added agony of the struggle itself, offering a chance for your mind to find rest.",
